---
/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   What withdrawal is actually like.

   Withdrawal appears on 35 of 571 Buena Vista calls (6.1% declarative), and 19
   calls (3.3%) carry explicit fear language — afraid, scared, nervous, dreading.
   That fear is what this page serves. The timeline is the vehicle; reassurance
   is the payload.

   ⚠ SAFETY — this page will be found by people considering stopping at home.
   Alcohol and benzodiazepine withdrawal can cause seizures and can be fatal.
   The hero therefore opens with an explicit "do not use this to detox alone",
   the two dangerous substances are visually flagged, and the FAQ closes with an
   emergency-room instruction. Do not remove any of those, and do not add
   home-taper guidance of any kind.

   Timings are established general clinical ranges, given as ranges and
   attributed to the substance rather than to a Buena Vista protocol. Our own
   detox length is stated separately where it is ours.

   Justification note: this page is driven more by search intent than call
   volume ("alcohol withdrawal timeline" is high-volume informational demand
   that feeds the detox money page). The call-driven work is largely done, so
   later pages increasingly rest on search rather than call evidence.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../../components/TopBar.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';

import WithdrawalHero from '../../components/withdrawal/WithdrawalHero.astro';
import BySubstance from '../../components/withdrawal/BySubstance.astro';
import WithdrawalQuestions from '../../components/withdrawal/WithdrawalQuestions.astro';

import Testimonials from '../../components/Testimonials.astro';
import VerifySection from '../../components/VerifySection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const title = 'Withdrawal Timelines: What to Expect | Buena Vista Health & Recovery, Chandler AZ';
const description =
  'How long alcohol, opioid, benzodiazepine and stimulant withdrawal lasts, which are dangerous to stop alone, and what a medically supervised detox actually involves. Call (888) 362-5576.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    ['How long does alcohol withdrawal last?',
     'Symptoms typically begin 6 to 24 hours after the last drink and are hardest around 24 to 72 hours. Alcohol withdrawal can cause seizures and delirium tremens and should be managed under medical supervision.'],
    ['Can I detox at home?',
     'Alcohol and benzodiazepine withdrawal can cause seizures and can be fatal, so neither should be attempted alone. Opioid withdrawal is rarely life-threatening but is severe enough that most home attempts end within a day.'],
    ['How long does opioid withdrawal last?',
     'It often begins within 8 to 24 hours of the last dose, sooner with fentanyl, and is worst during the first one to three days. Medication in a supervised detox substantially reduces the severity.'],
    ['Do stimulants cause physical withdrawal?',
     'Meth and cocaine do not produce the dangerous physical withdrawal alcohol does, so there is usually no separate detox stage. They produce exhaustion and a deep low that is heaviest in the first week.'],
  ].map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <TopBar />
  <Nav />

  <WithdrawalHero />
  <BySubstance />
  <Testimonials />
  <VerifySection />
  <WithdrawalQuestions />

  <FinalCTA />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} is:inline />
</Layout>
